---
title: Sweet Potato Syrup
description: Thin pumpkin-spiced syrup of blended, strained sweet potato and two sugars.
tags: [syrup]
course: condiment
icons: [potato, bottle-droplet, honey-pot]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: The Midwest Kitchen Blog
  url: https://www.themidwestkitchenblog.com/sweet-potato-syrup/
yield: 1 3/4%cups
prep time: 10m
cook time: 15m
---

Blend the @cooked and mashed sweet potato{1/2%cup} with @filtered water{1/2%cup} in a #blender{} until smooth.

Press through a #strainer{}, then add to a #pot{} with the remaining @&filtered water{1/2%cup}, @brown sugar{1/2%cup}, @white granulated sugar{1/2%cup}, @pumpkin spice mix{1%tsp}, and a @salt{1%pinch}.

Bring to a simmer over medium heat, then continue cooking for another ~simmer{5%minutes}. The syrup should have a thin consistency; it will thicken slightly as it cools.

Remove from the heat, then whisk in the @vanilla bean paste{1/2%tsp}(or vanilla extract). Allow to cool, then strain and transfer to a #mason jar{}.
